# Rust
/target
**/target

# Node (bb fork apps live here later)
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
**/dist/

# The workspace is pnpm (`packageManager` in `package.json` plus
# `pnpm-workspace.yaml`), so a root `bun.lock` is only ever what an accidental
# `bun install` at the repo root leaves behind. Anchored to the root on purpose:
# `tools/contract-export` is a real bun project whose lockfile is tracked, and a
# bare `bun.lock` pattern would reach it.
/bun.lock

# Vite's bundle report for the app's budget check: generated by every build,
# read by `check:bundle`, never committed.
apps/app/bundle-stats.json

# Local state
*.log
.DS_Store
.bb-dev/
.scratch/

# Playwright acceptance: reports, traces and the stack's own logs are run
# output, never sources.
e2e/test-results/
e2e/playwright-report/
e2e/blob-report/
e2e/*.log
